
2. Open the UI

Go to http://localhost:4000. A connection dialog opens on first load.

3. Fill in the connection

Field	Value
Name	local (anything)
Protocol	mqtt://
Host	mosquitto
Port	1883
Username / Password	leave blank
Validate certificate	off
Encryption (TLS)	off

Use mosquitto as the host, not localhost. The UI runs in its own container, so localhost would point at itself.

Click Save (the settings persist in the explorer_config volume), then Connect.

4. Check that it works

A $SYS branch should appear in the topic tree on the left. It holds the broker's own stats.
In the Publish panel on the right, enter topic test/hello, type a message, and click Publish. A test branch appears in the tree with your message.
Your client container, which subscribes to test/#, will also print it: docker logs -f <client-container-name>.

5. Optional: connect with TLS instead